\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139534264 17592186045417 true] [17592186416602 1072 #uuid "c8443228-62d0-53de-820f-4c2c2789eb2f" 13194139534264 17592186045417 true] [17592186416602 1074 "The change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C$ is a matrix whose respective columns are the coordinates of the vectors of $B$ relative to the basis $C.$ \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to C}=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 5 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139534264 17592186045417 true] [17592186416603 1068 #edb/ref 17592186416586 13194139534264 17592186045417 true] [17592186416603 1069 "q-113342" 13194139534264 17592186045417 true] [17592186416603 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534264 17592186045417 true] [17592186416603 1071 "Let $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}$ be a basis of ${R}^{2}$ and let $S$ be the standard basis of ${R}^{2}.$ \nFind the change-of-coordinates matrix ${P}_{B\\to S}$ from $B$ to $S$ if \n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139534264 17592186045417 true] [17592186416603 1072 #uuid "d6ffc405-f81c-5336-ad94-25ea55190ac1" 13194139534264 17592186045417 true] [17592186416603 1074 "Recall  that the standard basis of ${R}^{2}$ consists of the vectors ${e}_{1}$ and ${e}_{2},$ given by\n\n$$\n{e}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{e}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe components of the vectors of $B$ are just the coordinates relative to the standard basis:\n\n$$\n[{b}_{1}]_{S}=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,[{b}_{2}]_{S}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $S$ is a matrix whose respective columns are the coordinates of the vectors of $B$ relative to the basis $S.$ \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to S}=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139534264 17592186045417 true] [17592186416604 1068 #edb/ref 17592186416594 13194139534264 17592186045417 true] [17592186416604 1069 "q-36358" 13194139534264 17592186045417 true] [17592186416604 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139534264 17592186045417 true] [17592186416604 1071 "Let $B={[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]}$  be a basis of ${R}^{2}$ and $S$ is the standard basis of ${R}^{2}.$ Find the change-of-coordinates matrix from $S$ to $B.$" 13194139534264 17592186045417 true] [17592186416604 1072 #uuid "d9fbd56e-ebad-5e95-b783-252de92d505c" 13194139534264 17592186045417 true] [17592186416604 1074 "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ and $S$ as ${{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}$ and ${{e}_{1},{e}_{2}}$, respectively. Recall that the standard basis of ${R}^{2}$ consists of the vectors\n\n$$\n{e}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{e}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe change-of-coordinates matrix from $S$ to $B$ is a matrix whose columns are the coordinates of the vectors of $S$ relative to the basis $B.$\n\nHence, we need to find the coordinates of ${e}_{1}$ and ${e}_{2}$ relative to the basis $B.$ We can do this simultaneously by considering the matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}| & | & | & | \\\\ {b}_{1} & {b}_{2} & {e}_{1} & {e}_{2} \\\\ | & | & | & |\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we simply reduce the left-hand side to reduced row-echelon form using Gaussian elimination: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -6 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=(-\\frac{1}{2}){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the right-hand side, we obtain the change-of-coordinates matrix from $S$ to $B.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{P}_{S\\to B}=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139534264 17592186045417 true] [17592186416605 1068 #edb/ref 17592186416588 13194139534264 17592186045417 true] [17592186416605 1069 "q-113410" 13194139534264 17592186045417 true] [17592186416605 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534264 17592186045417 true] [17592186416605 1071 "The change-of-coordinates matrix from the basis $C$ to the basis $B$ is given by\n${P}_{C\\to B}=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}].$ Find the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C$  ." 13194139534264 17592186045417 true] [17592186416605 1072 #uuid "df33f267-a622-55d4-b6ca-07fa624cf0e9" 13194139534264 17592186045417 true] [17592186416605 1074 "The change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C$ is the inverse of the change-of-coordinates matrix from $C$ to $B.$ Therefore, we simply need to find the inverse of the given matrix.\n\nComputing the inverse of ${P}_{C\\to B}$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{B\\to C} & ={P}_{C\\to B}^{-1} \\\\  & ={[\\begin{aligned}4 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}]}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4\\cdot 4-5\\cdot 3}[\\begin{aligned}4 & -5 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =1\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}4 & -5 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & -5 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534264 17592186045417 true] [17592186416606 1068 #edb/ref 17592186416591 13194139534264 17592186045417 true] [17592186416606 1069 "q-81857" 13194139534264 17592186045417 true] [17592186416606 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534264 17592186045417 true] [17592186416606 1071 "The change-of-coordinates matrix from the basis $C$ to the basis $B$ is given by\n${P}_{C\\to B}=[\\begin{aligned}-6 & -5 \\\\ 5 & 4\\end{aligned}].$ Find the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C$  ." 13194139534264 17592186045417 true] [17592186416606 1072 #uuid "f1424ed2-0052-5fff-908d-b6551bfbb11a" 13194139534264 17592186045417 true] [17592186416606 1074 "The change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C$ is the inverse of the change-of-coordinates matrix from $C$ to $B.$ Therefore, we simply need to find the inverse of the given matrix.\n\nComputing the inverse of ${P}_{C\\to B}$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{B\\to C} & ={P}_{C\\to B}^{-1} \\\\  & ={[\\begin{aligned}-6 & -5 \\\\ 5 & 4\\end{aligned}]}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(-6)\\cdot 4-(-5)\\cdot 5}[\\begin{aligned}4 & 5 \\\\ -5 & -6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =1\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}4 & 5 \\\\ -5 & -6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 5 \\\\ -5 & -6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534264 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-02b7ac1d-4efd-51c0-b67d-14536d1d6f75" 17592186416524 "answer-07838b3a-5d21-5d4b-96ed-ad6dca8941c5" 17592186416525 "answer-08510d9c-0008-5b50-b913-170c103ba9c1" 17592186416526 "answer-1100f1bc-ed34-5a67-be8b-4cd9cbd023d1" 17592186416527 "answer-16853ab7-760d-5058-8e30-4207c809785e" 17592186416528 "answer-172c82bc-392e-5ec7-9deb-ddba9ffa9f17" 17592186416529 "answer-177497c8-e142-5d9e-abc1-becbb9a39472" 17592186416530 "answer-20235027-ad55-59fe-b1e5-b1705f888d17" 17592186416531 "answer-22bb294d-e537-5a35-8529-6eae6486a39b" 17592186416532 "answer-2344242d-6b96-5993-b8b0-de107b4279a2" 17592186416533 "answer-26ea652b-6e02-523c-b2ba-b95e1959da46" 17592186416534 "answer-2a7deef8-19c9-5a99-beb9-30ea6eec4a82" 17592186416535 "answer-367a8769-cd6a-5b95-9967-7c0f59ab154d" 17592186416536 "answer-3879c262-51c9-5503-937f-270c4a66ac2c" 17592186416537 "answer-3b26590d-792e-51f9-b6ee-9b92d34732ca" 17592186416538 "answer-3c3ac9c4-89a8-53e0-9f5b-0281ad0e261f" 17592186416539 "answer-3e6f0908-6c0d-5c24-87f5-821d61c33178" 17592186416540 "answer-40f45c93-6fe2-5f26-851c-9bd122ebd2a2" 17592186416541 "answer-419a7dcc-0ec9-5201-aaac-a0d26fd4a862" 17592186416542 "answer-4dd79918-775f-5123-b336-42017be04695" 17592186416543 "answer-50b04112-6a4b-5de0-8b36-cac7c5a0a40d" 17592186416544 "answer-54569e6c-7221-5713-add5-c98abf257a21" 17592186416545 "answer-57bd0aaf-7e37-5d1f-aa28-5056aba60ec5" 17592186416546 "answer-59e9f366-67f